## Key Notes & Methodology Flags

<div style="border-left:4px solid #1E3A8A;background:#EFF6FF;padding:8px 12px;margin:8px 0;border-radius:4px;">
<strong>1/n accounting change:</strong> IRDAI mandated 1/n premium/expense recognition w.e.f. 1 Oct 2024 for long-term products. The investor deck shows parallel "with 1/n" (statutory) and "without 1/n" (pre-change comparable) figures — e.g. GWP <span style="color:#1E3A8A;font-weight:600">₹6,762.2 Cr (with 1/n)</span> vs. ₹7,406.7 Cr (without 1/n), and Combined Ratio <span style="color:#F59E0B;font-weight:600">101.2% (with 1/n)</span> vs. 96.1% (without 1/n). Per instruction, the <strong>1/n statutory basis</strong> was used throughout to avoid mixing bases — the non-1/n figures were deliberately excluded.
</div>

<div style="border-left:4px solid #F59E0B;background:#FFFBEB;padding:8px 12px;margin:8px 0;border-radius:4px;">
<strong>EoM ratio vs. Expense ratio:</strong> The statutory Ratios Schedule reports "Expenses of Management Ratio" = <span style="font-weight:600">39.22%</span> (EoM/GDPI basis), differing from the deck's non-statutory "EoM as % of GWP" of 37.4% (footnoted "without 1/n"). The audited statutory figure was used per the sourcing hierarchy. The "Expense Ratio" (40.0%, with-1/n) is a separate combined-ratio component: Claims <span style="color:#EF4444;font-weight:600">61.2%</span> + Expense 40.0% = Combined <span style="color:#F59E0B;font-weight:600">▲ 101.2%</span> — consistent cross-check.
</div>

<div style="border-left:4px solid #22C55E;background:#F0FDF4;padding:8px 12px;margin:8px 0;border-radius:4px;">
<strong>PAT — dual-basis growth, both favorable:</strong> IGAAP PAT of <span style="color:#22C55E;font-weight:600">₹213.5 Cr ▲ 161% YoY</span> vs. IFRS PAT of <span style="color:#22C55E;font-weight:600">₹203.3 Cr ▲ 91% YoY</span>, per MD commentary on the earnings call. Both figures are independently disclosed and reconciled in the presentation/call — no discrepancy between bases.
</div>

- <span style="background:#F0FDF4;padding:2px 6px;border-radius:4px;color:#22C55E;font-weight:600">Solvency ratio 3.03x</span> — comfortably above the IRDAI regulatory minimum of 1.5x, flagged by the CFO on the earnings call as a "healthy level."
- <span style="color:#F59E0B;font-weight:600">Combined ratio of 101.22%</span> (statutory, with 1/n) indicates the underwriting result remains marginally above breakeven — a mixed signal versus the 96.1% non-1/n comparable, reflecting the transitional impact of the new premium-recognition rule rather than a deterioration in underlying loss experience.
- <span style="color:#1E3A8A;font-weight:600">AUM of ₹8,175.1 Cr</span> and <span style="color:#1E3A8A;font-weight:600">investment yield of 7.4%</span> were independently confirmed in both the written KPI disclosures and verbal CFO commentary, with no discrepancies found.
- **IRDAI NL-1/NL-2 statutory disclosure:** A dedicated public-disclosure PDF exists on the IRDAI disclosures page but was not separately re-extracted, since the audited Financial Results PDF already contains the full statutory Ratios Schedule (Reg 52(4)) with NWP, NEP, Net Worth, Solvency, Commission, Claims, EoM and Combined ratios — making it the authoritative, audited source, cross-checked against the investor presentation.
- **Completeness:** No line items required blanking — all 17 requested metrics were located in the audited statutory filing or the investor presentation/earnings call, each on a clearly labeled full-year (FY2025, year ended 31 March 2025) basis.</ans>
